# FVM and Dart formatting

## Run dart and flutter via FVM

All `dart` and `flutter` commands must be run through FVM (from project root).

- Use `fvm dart ...` instead of `dart ...`
- Use `fvm flutter ...` instead of `flutter ...`

Examples:

- `fvm flutter pub get`
- `fvm flutter test`
- `fvm dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs`
- `fvm dart format -l 100 .`

## Format after editing .dart files

After any changes to `.dart` files, invoke the **dart-format** skill (see [.cursor/skills/dart-format/SKILL.md](.cursor/skills/dart-format/SKILL.md)).

- Run from project root: `fvm dart format -l 100 .` or pass the path to the changed file(s).
- Use line length **100** and **FVM**; do not omit or change these.
